<title>NORWAY: TABLE-DnB H1 profits up.</title>
<headline>TABLE-DnB H1 profits up.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30.</p>
<p>				(millions of crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Net interest income	 2,144    vs   2,115</p>
<p> Other operating income    1,532    vs   1,419</p>
<p> Operating expenses	  2,333    vs   2,263</p>
<p> Pre-tax operating</p>
<p> profit before losses	1,343    vs   1,271</p>
<p> Pre-tax operating profit  1,505    vs   1,500</p>
<p> Profit for the period     1,494    vs   1,489</p>
<p> EPS (crowns)		  2,33     vs    2.32</p>
<p>NOTE -- Full name of Norway's biggest bank is Den norske Bank (DnB). It was expected to post a first-half 1997 pre-tax operating profit of about 1.55 billion crowns, according to a Reuters consensus poll of six analysts.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
